<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Sloping edge and slant height of a pyramid</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>{@ctx@} is a right pyramid VABCD on a rectangular base with AB = {@ll@} and BC = {@ww@} {@un@}. Its height VO is {@hh@} {@un@}. M is the midpoint of BC.</p><div style="text-align:center;" role="img" aria-label="A right pyramid VABCD on a rectangular base ABCD. O is the centre of the base, where the dashed diagonals AC and BD cross, and V is above O; VO is dotted. M is the midpoint of BC and N is the midpoint of AB. The hidden corner D and its edges are dashed.">
[[jsxgraph width="360px" height="280px"]]
(function() {
  var b = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox: [-1.2, 6.4, 8.9, -1.4], axis: false, grid: false, keepaspectratio: true,
    showNavigation: false, showCopyright: false, pan: {enabled: false}, zoom: {enabled: false}});
  // oblique projection: receding edges at 30 degrees, half length
  function P(x, y, z) { return [x + 0.5*y*Math.cos(Math.PI/6), z + 0.5*y*Math.sin(Math.PI/6)]; }
  var solid = {strokeColor: '#000000', strokeWidth: 2, fixed: true, highlight: false};
  var hid = {strokeColor: '#000000', strokeWidth: 1.5, dash: 2, fixed: true, highlight: false};
  var dot = {strokeColor: '#000000', strokeWidth: 1.5, dash: 1, fixed: true, highlight: false};
  var tx = {fixed: true, highlight: false, useMathJax: false, fontSize: 15, anchorX: 'middle', anchorY: 'middle'};
  var cx = 3.87, cy = 1.8;
  function lab(Q, s) { var dx = Q[0]-cx, dy = Q[1]-cy, r = Math.sqrt(dx*dx+dy*dy) || 1;
    b.create('text', [Q[0]+0.42*dx/r, Q[1]+0.42*dy/r, s], tx); }
  function seg(Q, R, o) { b.create('segment', [Q, R], o); }
  function mark(Q, R, S) { // right-angle mark at Q between QR and QS
    function u(X) { var dx = X[0]-Q[0], dy = X[1]-Q[1], r = Math.sqrt(dx*dx+dy*dy); return [0.3*dx/r, 0.3*dy/r]; }
    var a = u(R), c = u(S);
    b.create('polygon', [[Q[0]+a[0], Q[1]+a[1]], [Q[0]+a[0]+c[0], Q[1]+a[1]+c[1]], [Q[0]+c[0], Q[1]+c[1]]],
      {fixed: true, highlight: false, fillOpacity: 0, vertices: {visible: false},
       borders: {strokeColor: '#000000', strokeWidth: 1, fixed: true, highlight: false}});
  }
  // right pyramid VABCD on a rectangular base (shape only)
  var A = P(0,0,0), B = P(6,0,0), C = P(6,4,0), D = P(0,4,0), O = P(3,2,0), V = P(3,2,4.5), M = P(6,2,0), N = P(3,0,0);
  seg(A,B,solid); seg(B,C,solid); seg(V,A,solid); seg(V,B,solid); seg(V,C,solid);
  // hidden edges and the base diagonals dashed; the height VO dotted
  seg(A,D,hid); seg(D,C,hid); seg(V,D,hid); seg(A,C,hid); seg(B,D,hid); seg(V,O,dot);
  b.create('point', O, {fixed: true, highlight: false, size: 1.5, name: '', fillColor: '#000000', strokeColor: '#000000'});
  b.create('point', M, {fixed: true, highlight: false, size: 1.5, name: '', fillColor: '#000000', strokeColor: '#000000'});
  b.create('point', N, {fixed: true, highlight: false, size: 1.5, name: '', fillColor: '#000000', strokeColor: '#000000'});
  lab(A,'A'); lab(B,'B'); lab(C,'C'); lab(D,'D'); lab(V,'V');
  b.create('text', [M[0]+0.4, M[1], 'M'], tx); b.create('text', [N[0], N[1]-0.4, 'N'], tx);
  b.create('text', [O[0]-0.15, O[1]-0.4, 'O'], tx);
})();
[[/jsxgraph]]
</div><p>The diagram is not drawn to scale.</p><p>Find</p><p>(a) OA, the projection of VA on the base</p><div>[[input:ans1]] {@un@} [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) VA</p><div>[[input:ans2]] {@un@} [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) VM</p><div>[[input:ans3]] {@un@} [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div><p>Give lengths correct to 2 decimal places and angles correct to 1 decimal place. Keep full calculator accuracy until the final answer.</p>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) \(\mathrm{AC}^2 = {@ll@}^2 + {@ww@}^2 = {@SC@}\). O is the midpoint of AC, so \(\mathrm{OA}^2 = {@SC@} \div 4 = {@SA@}\) and OA = {@d2(OA)@} {@un@}.</p><p>(b) Triangle VOA has a right angle at O: \(\mathrm{VA}^2 = {@SA@} + {@hh@}^2 = {@SV@}\), so VA = {@d2(VA)@} {@un@}.</p><p>(c) OM is parallel to AB and half as long: OM = {@hl@} {@un@}. Triangle VOM has a right angle at O: \(\mathrm{VM}^2 = {@hl@}^2 + {@hh@}^2 = {@SM@}\), so VM = {@d2(VM)@} {@un@}. VA and VM are different lengths: VA goes to a corner, VM to the middle of a side.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
